          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "(Law)",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "A private arguing of cases for practice by students, as in the Inns of Court. [Obs.] Bolting cloth, wire, hair, silk, or other sieve cloth of different degrees of fineness; -- used by millers for sifting flour. McElrath. a receptacle.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
